AB  - Fully Homomorphic Encryption (FHE) provides a powerful mechanism to perform computations on encrypted data without revealing sensitive information. However, its significant computational overhead limits scalability, especially in dataintensive healthcare applications. This paper introduces an Adaptive Multi-Tier FHE Framework designed to balance efficiency and security by dynamically adjusting encryption parameters based on data sensitivity levels. The proposed architecture integrates differential privacy (DP) through controlled noise injection to strengthen privacy guarantees. Three distinct encryption tiers: high, medium, and low are defined to support logistic regression analysis on medical datasets, optimizing computational costs while maintaining confidentiality. The framework employs bootstrapping optimizations to mitigate noise accumulation and ensure stable model performance. This work contributes toward making scalable FHE-based privacy-preserving analytics practical for large-scale medical data settings.
