AB  - The dynamic, multi-tenant nature of network slices presented by rapid proliferation of 5G network slicing creates critical security vulnerabilities, especially the Distributed Denial-of-Service (DDoS) attacks. This paper presents a new Hybrid Adaptive Stacking Ensemble with Dynamic Confidence Gating (DCG), called AdaptiSlice-Guard which is built to detect the presence of DDoS attacks in the network slice of the 5G networks with privacy-preserving systems such as indicators of homomorphic encryption, GDPR compliance metrics, and data residency features. AdaptiSlice-Guard combines five different base learners (Random Forest, Extra Trees, Gradient Boosting, AdaBoost and SVM) using an entropy-based dynamic confidence gating algorithm and a Feature-Aware Gradient Boosting meta-learner, thus trained on a large scale dataset of 100 network slice records involving 25 security, privacy and performance parameters. The proposed ensemble was found to have the highest classification accuracy of 87.50% with an F1-score of 92.31% AUC-ROC of 94.87% greater than all the individual baseline classifiers such as Random Forest, SVM, Gradient Boosting, AdaBoost, Logistic Regression and Decision Tree. Extensive analysis with confusion matrices, ROC curve analysis, cross-validation, precision-recall analysis, and radar chart visualization proves that the adaptive ensemble of AdaptiSlice-Guard significantly reduces attack misclassification, which is inherent to single-algorithms systems. Such results declare AdaptiSlice-Guard an excellent privacy-conscious DDoS detection framework in 5G slicing, and have powerful implications in the next-generation network security, as well as in clinical-grade data protection. The framework is further validated on a healthcare-specific 5G network slicing dataset augmented with Electronic Health Record (EHR) access patterns, HL7/FHIR compliance indicators, and medical IoT device profiles, achieving 85.00% accuracy and 90.48% F1-score on the health domain, and 86.25% accuracy with 91.43% F1-score on a combined cross-domain dataset - confirming AdaptiSlice-Guard as a robust framework for protecting life-critical 5G healthcare network slices.
ER  - 

