AB  - The deep integration of cloud computing and deep learning has brought technological dividends to fields such as healthcare and finance. However, the placement of massive amounts of sensitive data in the cloud has triggered severe challenges in data security and privacy protection. To address core issues such as data privacy leakage, conflicts between encryption and computation, and the lack of cross-layer security protection, this paper proposes a Multi-Layer Secure Deep Learning model for cloud data (ML-SDL) with a multi-layer architecture design. This model constructs a multi-layer collaborative security architecture integrating the data layer, transmission layer, computing layer, model layer, and application layer. It incorporates cutting-edge privacy protection technologies such as efficient Format-Preserving Encryption, Proxy Re-Encryption, lattice-based homomorphic encryption, Partial Homomorphic Encryption, Secure Multi-Party Computation, Differential Privacy, and model watermarking, and designs efficient and secure distributed training/inference protocols. Experiments using the medical imaging dataset (COVIDx-CT) and the financial transaction dataset (IEEE-CIS Fraud Detection) verify the effectiveness of the ML-SDL architecture in resisting attacks such as gradient inversion and membership inference. While ensuring data security and privacy, it can maintain high model accuracy and computational efficiency, providing a feasible path for the secure implementation of deep learning applications in cloud environments.
ER  - 

